==Feedback Changes - January 12th==
As the Mahjarrat storyline continues, we've seen many of you complete Secrets of the North and move on to taking down the post-quest Phantom Muspah boss.

It's been lovely to read so much of your feedback about the quest itself, ranging from the puzzles, to the art, to the sound design, and the team are so glad you're enjoying the quest!

We'd like to address some of early feedback we've seen surrounding Secrets of the North, the Phantom Muspah, and some of the unique rewards added with yesterday's game update. Some of these have already been hotfixed and are now live in-game, alongside additional changes we'd like to make later today.

Yesterday, we released the following hotfixes:
* Fixed a bug where player death piles were appearing inside the Evelot fight instance.
* Adjusted the POH dummy to display Venator Bow max hits.
* Fixed a potential soft-lock for players who teleported out of the Ghorrock dungeon at a specific point in the quest.

Today, we'd like to make the following changes, so make sure to check out the whole post to stay informed on what's happening!

===Phantom Muspah===
In typical Old School fashion, players have started figuring out how to tackle Old School's newest boss as efficiently as possible to maximise your gains. As the dust begins to settle, we're making a few adjustments to the boss mechanics and loot.

;Mechanical Changes 
The first change we're making is to resolve a pesky bug with the Phantom Muspah's melee attacks that snuck past our QA team! This issue makes the Muspah always hit a 0 if it's moving towards you while attacking and you're praying Protect From Melee.

We're adjusting the melee behaviour slightly so that melee attack will be able to hit through prayer consistently, but we're reducing the attack's accuracy significantly to compensate. Additionally, melee attacks will be much easier to 'dodge' by staying on the move and keeping a bit of distance between you and the Phantom Muspah.

In addition to this, we've seen frustration at the inability to reliably catch freezes when using spells like Ice Barrage on the Phantom Muspah, especially for players not rocking best-in-slot Magic gear. We've opted to increase the accuracy of Ice spells against the Phantom Muspah by 10%, but this accuracy increase only applies when the boss is not already frozen.

While not strictly a mechanical change, we've seen reports of the Muspah skipping phases or ending up in empty instances if you manage to take it down before entering what is known as the 'Prayer Shield' phase. We're including some hotfixes that should prevent some of the more commonly reported bugs of this nature. If you run in to any other bizarre bugs or unusual interactions, make sure to let us know!

Lastly, we've seen reports that the Muspah is a phantom, but the Ectoplasmator has no use during the encounter. Next week, we'll be making the Phantom Muspah count as a spectral creature, so you can secure some extra Prayer gains!

;Loot Table
Following the release of Tombs of Amascut's drop mechanics last year, we committed ourselves to releasing unique drop rates within 2 weeks. We'd first like to say that we're planning to release the unique drop rates for Phantom Muspah in next week's newspost, scheduled for January 18th! Alongside this, we'll be letting Monster Examine reveal defensive stats with next week's game update.

In the meantime, we've seen some concerns about the quantity of loot up for grabs at the boss. While we're not looking to make any massive changes so close to release (especially with the price of unique items like Ancient Essence and Venator Shards still in flux), we agree that the loot is a little overtuned. We've made the following changes to the quantities of various items dropped by the boss:
* Yew Seed: Reduced from 3 to 2
* Palm Tree Seed: Reduced from 3 to 2
* Torstol Seed: Reduced from 6 to 5
* Grimy Snapdragon: Reduced from 38 to 31
* Grimy Toadflax: Reduced from 86 to 74
* Ranarr Seed (Uncommon): Reduced from 4 to 3
* Ranarr Seed (Rare): Reduced from 12 to 10

Additionally, we found that some players were effectively able to extend their trips indefinitely with the frequency of supply drops (e.g. Summer Pies, Sharks, potions). This is particularly the case for players in absolute Best-In-Slot gear who are already decimating the boss, and thus using less supplies in the first place. We've reduced the rate of these supply drops from 1/3.5 to 1/4.5, so that players should still be able to extend their trips but not live out the rest of their days within this frozen cave.

===Venator Bow===
Players lucky enough to have obtained a Venator Bow reported that it wasn't behaving as intended. The bow's max hits were moving from 100% to 50% to 25% with each bounce. The damage has been hotfixed today so that all bounces will correctly hit up to 66% of your max hit.

We also saw a lot of discussion around the decision to prevent the bow's usage in Barbarian Assault. While this decision was made with good intentions and to support a niche community of Barbarian Assault experts, we were surprised by the levels of engagement from the community on this. Many of you expressed frustrations about items being unusable in certain pieces of content and the confusion that brings, alongside believing metas and methods for various pieces of content should evolve alongside the rest of the game.

With this in mind, the Venator Bow is now able to be used within Barbarian Assault.

===Saturated Heart===
Let's keep things simple to start: you can now use your Saturated Heart while in the bank interface.

We also saw many of you ask for us to make the Saturated Heart tradeable, for a number of good reasons. Chief among them, both the Imbued Heart and Ancient Essence are tradeable, so it makes sense for the Saturated Heart to act the same. Additionally, the heart being tradeable means GIM players and people trading the Heart between team members in some PvM encounters don't feel as though they're losing out in some scenarios by upgrading.

Unfortunately it's not possible for us to hotfix this, but we'll be making the Saturated Heart tradeable with next week's game update.

That's all we have for today! We're still discussing your feedback around other changes from yesterday's update, namely the visuals for the Fairy Ring and the arrangement of bonuses on the Equipment Interface. We don't have anything concrete to add just yet, but we'll let you know once we've got more to share!

